@startuml sequence_reaction
title Sequence Diagram: Comment Reaction (Like)

actor User as user
participant Browser as browser
participant Django as django
participant CommentReactionView as view
participant Comment as comment
participant CommentReaction as reaction
participant Database as db

== User Clicks Reaction Button ==

user -> browser: Click reaction button (e.g., thumbs up)
activate browser
browser -> django: POST /comment/<comment_id>/react
activate django
django -> view: CommentReactionView.post()
activate view

== Authentication Check ==

view -> view: Check if user.is_authenticated
activate view

alt User Not Authenticated
    view --> django: JsonResponse(error=Authentication required)
    deactivate view
    django --> browser: HTTP 401 Unauthorized
    deactivate django
    browser -> user: Show login prompt
    deactivate browser
else User Authenticated
    view -> comment: Get comment by id
    activate comment
    comment --> view: Return comment
    deactivate comment

    view -> reaction: CommentReaction.objects.get_or_create(comment=comment, user=user, reaction_type=type)
    activate reaction
    reaction -> db: Check if reaction exists
    activate db

    alt Reaction Already Exists
        db --> reaction: Return existing reaction
        deactivate db
        reaction -> reaction: Delete reaction (toggle off)
        reaction --> view: reaction, created=False
    else Reaction Does Not Exist
        reaction -> db: INSERT INTO comments_commentreaction
        activate db
        db --> reaction: Return success
        deactivate db
        reaction --> view: reaction, created=True
    end

    reaction --> view: Return reaction result
    deactivate reaction

    view -> comment: comment.get_reactions_summary(user)
    activate comment
    comment -> db: SELECT reaction_type, COUNT(*) FROM comments_commentreaction WHERE comment_id=<id> GROUP BY reaction_type
    activate db
    db --> comment: Return reaction statistics
    deactivate db
    comment --> view: Return reactions_data
    deactivate comment

    view --> django: JsonResponse({success: True, action: added/removed, reactions: reactions_data})
    deactivate view
    django --> browser: HTTP 200 OK
    deactivate django
    browser -> user: Update UI with new reaction count
    deactivate browser
end

@enduml
